2026-09-27T03:28:07.4545077Z Description:
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4545538Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4545939Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4547050Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4547843Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4547932Z Update Note
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4548131Z ===========
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4548429Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4548695Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4548785Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4548992Z ================
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4549129Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4549281Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4549633Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4549833Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4549946Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4550211Z ====================================
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4550373Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4550518Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4551176Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4551507Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4552135Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4552641Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4552764Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4553195Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4553697Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4553950Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4554237Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4554611Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4554694Z Packages
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4554881Z ========
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4554990Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4556176Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4557373Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4557586Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4558028Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4558458Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4558988Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4559502Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4559901Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4632623Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4633405Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4633872Z ==========================
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4634119Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4635677Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4637471Z 
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4638346Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4639649Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T03:28:07.4639969Z 
